  "name": "CD4 Absolute Count",
  "code": "CD4ABS",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul><li>Low count: A low Absolute CD4 Count indicates that the individual's immune function is compromised, and they may be at increased risk for infections and other complications. The severity of immune suppression depends on the degree of CD4 T-lymphocyte depletion, with severe immune suppression typically associated with counts below 200 cells per microliter. Low Absolute CD4 Counts are commonly seen in individuals with HIV/AIDS and other conditions that affect the immune system.</li><li>High count: A high Absolute CD4 Count is rare and may indicate a hyperactive immune system, such as in certain autoimmune disorders or chronic infections.</li></ul>",
